<h2 id="operations">Buttons, remote commands and sirens</h2>

Button and input-button are momentary operations. A last-pressed timestamp records activation, not a persistent on state. Use an action verb that names the verified operation. A counter reset must show the actual reset target when known. The same-looking button may have very different consequences, so do not infer behaviour from a generic icon.

Remote, infrared and radio-frequency entities can expose commands whose feedback varies by integration. Show only supplied/verified capabilities. A transmitted command does not establish that a receiver acted. Do not invent power, volume, pairing or learning controls solely because a domain exists. Siren activation can affect people nearby; keep the real target, supported tone/duration and confirmation policy visible. Native permissions remain authoritative.

